A clearing break moves whatever follows past the clearance, and leaves
the text of the line it ends in place, in every writing mode. Ladybird
extends that line to the clearance, but mirrors a vertical-lr line’s
content within the content’s own extent, so the text stays put. WebKit
records the clearance as the clear gap after the last line, in
InlineFormattingContext::updateLayoutStateWithLineLayoutResult(). Blink
adds the line’s LayoutResult::ClearanceAfterLine() to the block offset
of what follows, in BlockLayoutAlgorithm::ComputeInflowPosition(). And
Gecko’s nsBlockFrame::PlaceLine() moves BlockReflowState::mBCoord with
ClearFloats() for a line whose FloatClearTypeAfter() is set. None of
them changes the line’s size, so the text in it stays in place.
